+# Storage usage
+
+`Account#bytes_used` and `Board#bytes_used` read persistent background-calculated
+byte totals. New accounts and boards return zero. The recurring
+`Storage::Change.process_later` task runs every minute; pending batches continue
+processing until caught up. Reads do not scan attachments or enqueue jobs.
+
+Counted storage consists of card images and Active Storage embeds in board
+public descriptions, card descriptions, and comment bodies (including drafts).
+Each attachment reference counts its blob's `byte_size`. Reusing a blob in two
+places counts both references; repeating it within the same rich text counts the
+single underlying attachment. Avatars, variants, previews, exports, imports,
+unattached uploads, remote URLs, and non-file Action Text attachables are excluded.
+
+## Updates and concurrency
+
+Attachment changes transactionally invalidate their owning board, card, or
+comment. Repeated changes coalesce into one versioned row per owner. Writers
+never update or lock an account-wide storage counter.
+
+Workers reconcile at most 100 owners per transaction, using indexed SQL sums
+for only those owners' attachments. Each owner's last accounted state is stored
+in `storage_entries`. Net deltas update the board and account totals once per
+batch. Card moves transfer already-counted comment usage along with the card;
+subsequent pending comment changes resolve the card's current board.
+
+The account's `storage_totals` row serializes workers. Source snapshots, totals,
+and acknowledgement of the processed invalidation versions commit together.
+Concurrent edits remain pending; retries and duplicate jobs do not double-count.
+A failed enqueue cannot lose changes because the recurring task discovers the
+durable invalidations. Deletion uses invalidation IDs, not jobs that need to
+load deleted cards, boards, comments, or attachments.
+
+## Existing data and imports
+
+The recurring task automatically schedules background backfills for accounts
+without a completed backfill. Backfills traverse records in bounded batches,
+not attachment objects, and use the same reconciliation path as live changes.
+Completed imports also force a backfill since bulk insertion bypasses callbacks.
+
+To recalculate existing records after maintenance that bypasses callbacks:
+
+```ruby
+Storage::BackfillJob.perform_later(account, force: true)
+```
+
+Storage tables are derived data and are not included in account exports.
